{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","id":"0998bb760ccdbb19024fc324","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum%40arm.com/","channels":["linux-arch"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum@arm.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum%40arm.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum@arm.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 6/9] mm: convert PTE table entry to pte","messages":{"99eac5ca-d5c6-4777-b16c-5a20fae95f5d@arm.com":{"id":"99eac5ca-d5c6-4777-b16c-5a20fae95f5d@arm.com","messageId":"99eac5ca-d5c6-4777-b16c-5a20fae95f5d@arm.com","references":["20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum@arm.com","20260806083926.1807279-7-usama.anjum@arm.com","fab9fc78-1e1d-4d5b-a9ca-92f3ebd04108-agordeev@linux.ibm.com","5c329236-7761-4e42-a549-b822e43b4358@arm.com","2599c5b3-e8ac-4865-993b-d41e6f060d52-agordeev@linux.ibm.com","f0b0dacb-fb83-4402-b0ea-30072727dfd7@arm.com","e9de4158-b829-471b-980c-1999959bbc48@kernel.org"],"missingAncestorIds":["e9de4158-b829-471b-980c-1999959bbc48@kernel.org","f0b0dacb-fb83-4402-b0ea-30072727dfd7@arm.com","2599c5b3-e8ac-4865-993b-d41e6f060d52-agordeev@linux.ibm.com","5c329236-7761-4e42-a549-b822e43b4358@arm.com","fab9fc78-1e1d-4d5b-a9ca-92f3ebd04108-agordeev@linux.ibm.com","20260806083926.1807279-7-usama.anjum@arm.com","20260806083926.1807279-1-usama.anjum@arm.com"],"author":{"name":"Muhammad Usama Anjum","address":"usama.anjum@arm.com"},"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T10:06:20.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T10:06:20.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 6/9] mm: convert PTE table entry to pte","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 11/08/2026 1:11 pm, David Hildenbrand (Arm) wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On 8/10/26 13:06, Muhammad Usama Anjum wrote:"},{"depth":2,"text":"On 10/08/2026 7:44 am, Alexander Gordeev wrote:"},{"depth":3,"text":"On Fri, Aug 07, 2026 at 05:26:04PM +0100, Muhammad Usama Anjum wrote:"},{"depth":4,"text":"Yes, this is particular line is for non MMU. In this case, CONIFG_ARCH_HAS_HW_PTE"},{"depth":4,"text":"would never be defined. Hence hw_pte_t is just pte_t and direct dereference is"},{"depth":4,"text":"allowed. I'd thought a lot about it; is better to leave direct dereference here"},{"depth":4,"text":"or use some helper. Then used __pte_from_hw() was already being used in generic"},{"depth":4,"text":"ptep_get()."},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"But in case CONIFG_ARCH_HAS_HW_PTE=n __pte_from_hw() is still gets called."},{"depth":3,"text":"That looks inconsistent to me. Why not just call ptep_deref() (see below)?"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Agreed. Calling __pte_from_hw() directly exposes the representation"},{"depth":2,"text":"conversion at the call site. I will introduce ptep_deref() and use it"},{"depth":2,"text":"here."},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":4,"text":"There are only two users of __pte_from_hw() at this time. "},{"depth":4,"text":""},{"depth":4,"text":"ptep_get_sw() or ptep_get_deref() is better name here?"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"ptep_deref() would be it."},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"Do you agree to the suggested API requirements?"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Yes. hw_pte_t * identifies storage containing hardware-formatted PTEs,"},{"depth":2,"text":"regardless of whether it is attached. ptep_get() is used for attached"},{"depth":2,"text":"entries and may provide additional architecture-specific handling."},{"depth":2,"text":"ptep_deref() is used for unattached entries and performs only the raw"},{"depth":2,"text":"storage-to-value conversion."},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"For review, this patch would become:"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"diff --git a/include/linux/hugetlb.h b/include/linux/hugetlb.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"index bc0b9c65aa1d0..ce900d2652d91 100644"},{"depth":2,"text":"--- a/include/linux/hugetlb.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"+++ b/include/linux/hugetlb.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"@@ -1283,7 +1283,7 @@ static inline pte_t huge_ptep_clear_flush(struct vm_area_struct *vma,"},{"depth":2,"text":" #ifdef CONFIG_MMU"},{"depth":2,"text":" \treturn ptep_get(ptep);"},{"depth":2,"text":" #else"},{"depth":2,"text":"-\treturn *ptep;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+\treturn ptep_deref(ptep);"},{"depth":2,"text":" #endif"},{"depth":2,"text":" }"},{"depth":2,"text":" "},{"depth":2,"text":"diff --git a/include/linux/pgtable.h b/include/linux/pgtable.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"index 1768421755a9c..08613593f3320 100644"},{"depth":2,"text":"--- a/include/linux/pgtable.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"+++ b/include/linux/pgtable.h"},{"depth":2,"text":"@@ -490,6 +490,13 @@ static inline int pudp_set_access_flags(struct vm_area_struct *vma,"},{"depth":2,"text":" #endif /* CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE */"},{"depth":2,"text":" #endif"},{"depth":2,"text":" "},{"depth":2,"text":"+#ifndef ptep_deref"},{"depth":2,"text":"+static inline pte_t ptep_deref(hw_pte_t *ptep)"},{"depth":2,"text":"+{"},{"depth":2,"text":"+\treturn __pte_from_hw(*ptep);"},{"depth":2,"text":"+}"},{"depth":2,"text":"+#endif"},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":" #ifndef ptep_get"},{"depth":2,"text":" static inline pte_t ptep_get(hw_pte_t *ptep)"},{"depth":2,"text":" {"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I mean, how many such users do we expect? 1? :)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Why have a helper for that then, that seems to encourage it's use, when really"},{"depth":1,"text":"people should be using ptep_get() ?"}],"lineCount":70,"maximumDepth":4},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"There is only 1 direct dereference case and even that is for non-MMU case.\nThat's really good point. I'll keep using __pte_from_hw() and put a comment\nin huge_ptep_clear_flush() that use of this must be avoided at all cost. An\nAPI can be introduced in case more users arrive."},{"kind":"signature","text":"Thanks,\nUsama","lineCount":2}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"e9de4158-b829-471b-980c-1999959bbc48@kernel.org"}},"rootIds":["99eac5ca-d5c6-4777-b16c-5a20fae95f5d@arm.com"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["99eac5ca-d5c6-4777-b16c-5a20fae95f5d@arm.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}